[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Vehicles/images/banner.jpg?v=2[/img]

[b]An early test build.[/b] Dazed Vehicles is being tested with plain coloured boxes while the physics are worked out. Real models and art come later, so it is not ready for a normal game yet. Please report problems in the Discussions tab.

[table]
[tr][td][b]Game version[/b][/td][td]Build 42 only (42.0+)[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Requires[/b][/td][td][b]Dazed Core[/b] 1.6.1 or later (subscribe to it too)[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Multiplayer[/b][/td][td]Untested. The server and every player need it[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Mod ID[/b][/td][td]DazedVehicles[/td][/tr]
[/table]

[h2]What is in it[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Armored bus (Dawn of the Dead style):[/b] a stock shuttle bus with 10 seats and a big luggage bay, found at airports and transit stops. Rarely one turns up already armored, or you can bolt on window cages, side skirts, a ram with a saw rig, a roof rack and more yourself.
[*][b]Dash Rattlesnake:[/b] an early-90s V10 roadster and coupe. Quick and twitchy, found at sports-car spots and luxury dealerships.
[*][b]Two-wheelers:[/b] a bicycle and a motorcycle with a sidecar, for physics testing only. They do not spawn in the world.
[/list]

[h2]Not known yet[/h2]
Whether all ten bus seats work and sync in multiplayer, how the armor looks and holds up, and whether bicycle-wide vehicles can ride and fit through doors. That is what this build is for.

[i]Mod ID: DazedVehicles · Version 0.0.1[/i]
